    [BugFix][Ops] Make DSA block size a Triton constexpr object (#18079)
    
    A type annotation is not visible inside @triton.jit. Construct
    tl.constexpr directly so the kernel can read the block size.
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    BUILD_LOCAL_METADATA_BLOCK_SIZE in vllm_ascend/ops/triton/dsa_cp.py was
    declared as a type annotation:
    ```sh
    BUILD_LOCAL_METADATA_BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr = 1024
    ```
    Triton does not see that global inside @triton.jit. This PR constructs a
    real constexpr object so the kernel can read the block size:
    ```sh
    BUILD_LOCAL_METADATA_BLOCK_SIZE = tl.constexpr(1024)
    ```
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
